# ARC-0008 stage 6 (levels 11-12): The Wheel Stops, Fortune's Reach, Tier III (Aspect of Anticipation), Ready: Foreseen.
# Spec: 50_ENGINEERING/55_Implementation_Specs/SPEC_ARC-0008.md (stage 6); decisions SP112-SP114. Applied with
#   perl 80_TOOLS_AND_PIPELINE/82_Automation/stats/stats_add.pl <this> --apply      ([fechado] ARC-0008)
# No `using`: every field is written. Numbers: 25.01/SPL_Kingmaker_TheWheelStops (level 6, 2 turns, 9 m),
# 25.01/SPL_Kingmaker_Foreseen (once per round: the reaction cost).

@loca KM_WHEEL_STOPS_NAME The Wheel Stops
@loca KM_WHEEL_STOPS_DESC Stop Fortune's wheel. It doesn't turn at the start of your next [1] turns.
@loca KM_WHEEL_STOPS_EXTRA While the Wheel is stopped, at the start of each of your turns every Fallen enemy within [1] of a Reigning ally suffers its Crossing.<br><br>Once per <LSTag Tooltip="LongRest">Long Rest</LSTag>.
@loca KM_WHEEL_STOPPED_DESC Held on Fortune's wheel: the Wheel doesn't turn it while it is stopped.
@loca KM_REACH_NAME Fortune's Reach
@loca KM_REACH_DESC Your Crossings no longer need an ally nearby: an enemy that becomes Fallen while any ally on the Wheel is Reigning suffers its Crossing.
@loca KM_ANTICIPATION_NAME Aspect of Anticipation
@loca KM_ANTICIPATION_DESC Your allies never touch the bottom of the Wheel: instead of becoming Fallen, they stay Falling for one more turn. You can also prepare <LSTag Type="Spell" Tooltip="Shout_Arcana_Created_Aspect_ReadyForeseen">Foreseen</LSTag>.
@loca KM_AWAKENED_III_NAME 10 - Wheel of Fortune: Awakened III
@loca KM_AWAKENED_III_DESC Tyche: creatures you set on the Wheel enter one position ahead. Allies you crown begin Reigning, and enemies you cast down begin Fallen.<br><br>Nemesis: when an enemy with Hubris suffers its Crossing, every enemy within [1] of it that is Falling drops to Fallen.<br><br>Aspect of Anticipation: your allies never touch the bottom of the Wheel; they stay Falling for one more turn instead of becoming Fallen.
@loca KM_READY_FORESEEN_NAME Ready: Foreseen
@loca KM_READY_FORESEEN_DESC Watch the Wheel. Until combat ends you can react with <LSTag Type="Spell" Tooltip="Interrupt_Arcana_Aspect_Foreseen">Foreseen</LSTag>.
@loca KM_FORESEEN_NAME Foreseen
@loca KM_FORESEEN_DESC When an enemy on the Wheel is about to attack you or an ally, push it one position onward before the blow lands, if it is Reigning or Falling.
@loca KM_FORESEEN_EXTRA You saw it coming.
@loca KM_FORESEEN_READY_DESC Watching the Wheel. Can react with Foreseen until combat ends.

